.TH WEATHER-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-18" "weather-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
weather-revamped \- weather from wttr.in in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weather-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.RI [ place ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B weather-revamped
shows the weather wttr.in reports for one place in the tmux status line:
the condition and the temperature, what it feels like, the wind, the
humidity, the pressure and its trend, the precipitation and the rain
chance, the UV index, the dew point, the sun, the moon, today and
tomorrow, and an alert line from an address of your own.
.PP
The entry point
.B weather-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the popup key in one tmux call
and replaces #{weather} and every #{weather_name} placeholder in status-left
and status-right.
.PP
A status call prints the stored reading at once. When the reading is older
than the fetch interval it starts one fetch in the background, so the status
line never waits. An answer that says the location is unknown is dropped and
the last reading stays. Run with no command on a terminal, the tool offers a
menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the popup key, and the refresh key when one is set, and replace the status placeholders now. In the options render mode it also starts the daemon.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B status
Print one placeholder from the stored reading, for the first location or for the place given after the name: weather, temp, feels_like, wind, humidity, pressure, pressure_trend, precip, rain_chance, umbrella, uv, uv_color, dew_point, dew_comfort, moon, sunrise, sunset, forecast, today_high, today_low, tomorrow_high, tomorrow_low, condition_icon, condition_tint, color, icon, stale_color or alert. A reading older than the fetch interval starts one fetch in the background.
.TP
.B refresh
Fetch the weather now, for the first location or for the place given, store the reading and say what wttr.in answered. It fails when wttr.in gives no reading.
.TP
.B card
Print one row per part of the reading: the place, the weather now, the wind, the humidity, the pressure, the UV index, the dew point, the precipitation, the rain chance, the sun, the moon, today and tomorrow, and the alert when alerts are on. A stale reading is fetched first.
.TP
.B popup
Open the card in a tmux popup that closes on Enter. The popup key runs it. It needs tmux 3.2 or later.
.TP
.B daemon
Fetch every stale location and publish every placeholder the status line uses, once per tick, until another daemon takes over or the tmux server ends. apply starts it in the options render mode.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, curl, the age of the stored reading, the notifier, the key it found bound, gum and the core tools. Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-units
or
.BR \-\-fetch\-minutes .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on the popup key and on every status call.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI WEATHER_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR WEATHER_REVAMPED_UNITS .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B WEATHER_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B WEATHER_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B WEATHER_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B WEATHER_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing. An on
or off option also reads 1, yes and true as on, and 0, no and false as off.
An option that holds any other value takes its default, and doctor names it.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_popup_key
The prefix key that opens the forecast popup. off binds nothing. The default is M\-w, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_refresh_key
A prefix key that fetches the weather at once, in the background. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_location
The city or place to ask wttr.in about. Empty lets wttr.in locate the machine by its address. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_locations
Several places separated by semicolons. The first one fills the placeholders, and it outranks the single location. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_units
m for Celsius and km/h, u for Fahrenheit and mph; f, fahrenheit and imperial are read as u. The default is m.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_fetch_minutes
How many minutes a reading stays fresh before the next fetch, 1 or more. The default is 15.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_hide_units
on drops the C or F from #{weather_temp}. The default is off.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_alerts
on fetches the alert address after each reading. The default is off.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_alert_url
The address the alert line comes from, with {loc} replaced by the place. Its first line that is not empty is the alert. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_alert_prefix
Text printed before #{weather_alert}. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_notify
1 sends a desktop notification when a location gets a new alert. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_umbrella_text
What #{weather_umbrella} prints once the rain chance reaches the threshold, with {chance} replaced by the chance. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_umbrella_threshold
The rain chance, in percent, from which the umbrella text shows. The default is 50.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_stale_color
The style #{weather_stale_color} prints once the last answer is older than three fetch intervals. The default is #[dim].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_pressure_delta
The change in hPa beyond which the pressure counts as rising or falling. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_pressure_rising
What #{weather_pressure_trend} prints when the pressure rose. The default is ^.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_pressure_falling
What #{weather_pressure_trend} prints when the pressure fell. The default is v.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_pressure_steady
What #{weather_pressure_trend} prints when the pressure held. The default is =.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_uv_low_color
The style #{weather_uv_color} prints for a UV index of 0 to 2. The default is #[fg=green].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_uv_moderate_color
The style #{weather_uv_color} prints for a UV index of 3 to 5. The default is #[fg=yellow].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_uv_high_color
The style #{weather_uv_color} prints for a UV index of 6 to 7. The default is #[fg=colour208].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_uv_very_high_color
The style #{weather_uv_color} prints for a UV index of 8 to 10. The default is #[fg=red].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_uv_extreme_color
The style #{weather_uv_color} prints for a UV index of 11 and up. The default is #[fg=magenta].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_freezing_color
The style #{weather_color} prints at below 0 degrees Celsius. The default is #[fg=blue].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_cold_color
The style #{weather_color} prints at 0 to 9 degrees Celsius. The default is #[fg=cyan].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_cool_color
The style #{weather_color} prints at 10 to 17 degrees Celsius. The default is #[fg=green].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_comfortable_color
The style #{weather_color} prints at 18 to 23 degrees Celsius. The default is #[fg=green].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_hot_color
The style #{weather_color} prints at 24 to 31 degrees Celsius. The default is #[fg=yellow].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_very_hot_color
The style #{weather_color} prints at 32 and up degrees Celsius. The default is #[fg=red].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_freezing_icon
What #{weather_icon} prints at below 0 degrees Celsius. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_cold_icon
What #{weather_icon} prints at 0 to 9 degrees Celsius. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_cool_icon
What #{weather_icon} prints at 10 to 17 degrees Celsius. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_comfortable_icon
What #{weather_icon} prints at 18 to 23 degrees Celsius. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_hot_icon
What #{weather_icon} prints at 24 to 31 degrees Celsius. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_very_hot_icon
What #{weather_icon} prints at 32 and up degrees Celsius. The default is none.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_show_condition_icon
off empties #{weather_condition_icon}. The default is on.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_clear_condition_icon
What #{weather_condition_icon} prints for a clear sky. The default is a Nerd Font Material Design glyph.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_clouds_condition_icon
What #{weather_condition_icon} prints for a clouds sky. The default is a Nerd Font Material Design glyph.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_rain_condition_icon
What #{weather_condition_icon} prints for a rain sky. The default is a Nerd Font Material Design glyph.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_snow_condition_icon
What #{weather_condition_icon} prints for a snow sky. The default is a Nerd Font Material Design glyph.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_storm_condition_icon
What #{weather_condition_icon} prints for a storm sky. The default is a Nerd Font Material Design glyph.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_fog_condition_icon
What #{weather_condition_icon} prints for a fog sky. The default is a Nerd Font Material Design glyph.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_clear_tint
The style #{weather_condition_tint} prints for a clear sky. The default is #[fg=yellow].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_clouds_tint
The style #{weather_condition_tint} prints for a clouds sky. The default is #[fg=brightblack].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_rain_tint
The style #{weather_condition_tint} prints for a rain sky. The default is #[fg=blue].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_snow_tint
The style #{weather_condition_tint} prints for a snow sky. The default is #[fg=white].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_storm_tint
The style #{weather_condition_tint} prints for a storm sky. The default is #[fg=magenta].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_fog_tint
The style #{weather_condition_tint} prints for a fog sky. The default is #[fg=brightblack].
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_render
jobs runs one status call per placeholder; options reads tmux options the daemon fills, so a status refresh starts no process. The default is jobs.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_interval
Seconds between two ticks of the daemon in the options render mode. The default is 60.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_fixed_width
on pads #{weather_temp} on the left to five characters. The default is off.
.TP
.B @weather_revamped_temp_width
The width #{weather_temp} is padded to on the left. It wins over the fixed width, and a longer value is never cut. The default is none.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The stored reading of a place lives in
.BI @weather_revamped_value_ place
with the time of the last try, in
.BI @weather_revamped_ place _ok_ts ,
the time of the last answer, in
.BI @weather_revamped_ place _pressure_prev
and in
.BI @weather_revamped_alert_ place ,
where the place has every character other than a plain letter, a digit or an
underscore written as an underscore, and no place is auto. apply records
the placeholders the status line uses in
.BR @weather_revamped_published ,
the daemon writes each one to
.BI @weather_revamped_out_ name
and keeps its process id in
.BR @weather_revamped_ticker_pid .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR gum (1)
